'' =============================================================================
'' Single-Step Debugger Test Program 12 — Multi-COG debugging (PURE PASM2)
''
'' Covers Test Plan test:
''   Test 12 — Per-cog debugger windows, independent stepping, COGBRK
''
'' PASM-only program: cog 0 boots directly into this DAT at $000 (like the other
'' DAT-only tests 3, 6-11), so DEBUG_MAIN breaks on the FIRST instruction — no
'' Spin2 interpreter or cogspin indirection in the way. A Spin2-based counterpart
'' lives in test12a_multicog.spin2.
''
'' Behavior:
''   entry (cog 0) does a benign NOP (the first break lands here, matching the
''   working DAT tests), then COGINITs cog 1 loading its PASM from hub (@cog1code).
''   With DEBUG_COGINIT=1 the P2 debug interrupt fires on the launched cog's first
''   instruction, so cog 1 breaks on startup and a second window opens. Each cog
''   then increments its OWN counter in a tight loop, so the two windows step
''   fully independently.
''
''   CONSTRUCTION NOTES (learned the hard way on HW):
''   • Per-cog counters are hub-backed `long 0` cells, NOT `res` — a `res` reserves
''     a cog register but emits no hub bytes, so cog 1's image would land on top of
''     cog 0's counter slot. `long 0` keeps the two cog images in DISJOINT hub
''     regions (cog 1's image is `orgh`-aligned after cog 0's block).
''   • COGINIT uses a plain `#` (9-bit) source, NOT `##` — @cog1code fits in 9 bits,
''     so this avoids an AUGS prefix as cog 0's executed instruction.
''
'' Expected on hardware:
''   1. Cog 0 breaks at `entry` (the NOP) — "Debugger - Cog 0" window.
''   2. Single-step cog 0 through the NOP + coginit → cog 1 launches and breaks —
''      "Debugger - Cog 1" window opens.
''   3. Stepping one window advances only that cog (x in cog 0, y in cog 1).
'' =============================================================================
CON
  _clkfreq = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_MAIN = 1
  DEBUG_COGINIT = 1

DAT
' ── Cog 0 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
              org     0
entry         nop                             ' benign first break (matches the working DAT tests)
              coginit #1, #@cog1code          ' load & start Cog 1 from hub @cog1code (plain #, no AUGS)
.loop         add     x, #1
              jmp     #.loop
x             long    0                        ' hub-backed counter (see CONSTRUCTION NOTES)

' ── Cog 1 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Self-contained hub image, assembled to run at cog $000, residing at @cog1code.
' `orgh` puts it on a clean hub long boundary, disjoint from cog 0's block.
' Breaks on its first instruction via the debug-on-coginit interrupt.
              orgh
cog1code
              org     0
c1            add     y, #1
              jmp     #c1
y             long    0                        ' hub-backed counter (see CONSTRUCTION NOTES)
